              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "x(t)=2e^{-4t}u(t),\\qquad h(t)=7e^{-4t}u(t)",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ],
            "choices": [],
            "correct_choice_labels": [],
            "correct_answer": "(x*h)(t)=14t $e^{-4t}$$u(t)$",
            "answer_explanation_blocks": [
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The two exponentials have the same decay rate, so the only new feature is the product of the leading scale factors.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "(x*h)(t)=u(t)\\int_0^t \\left(2e^{-4\\tau}\\right)\\left(7e^{-4(t-\\tau)}\\right)\\,d\\tau",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "Multiply the constants first, then use the repeated-exponent cancellation.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "\\left(2e^{-4\\tau}\\right)\\left(7e^{-4(t-\\tau)}\\right)=14e^{-4\\tau-4t+4\\tau}=14e^{-4t}",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "paragraph",
                "text": "The integral over the causal overlap interval contributes the length t, and the final unit step records the zero-output region for $t<0$.",
                "latex": "",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              },
              {
                "block_type": "display-math",
                "text": "",
                "latex": "(x*h)(t)=u(t)\\int_0^t 14e^{-4t}\\,d\\tau=14t e^{-4t}u(t)",
                "image_slot_id": ""
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
